From 6aa2d5a4076016bf974757595135163e9086056a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 345/488] soh: name the 15 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_zl1.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 15 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Zl1/z_en_zl1.c.

  * D_80B4E61C -> sEyeTextures
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the eye textures Zelda's blink cycles through,
    indexed by the blink frame.

  * D_80B4E62C -> sMouthTextures
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the mouth textures, indexed by the mouth
    state; only the neutral one exists.

  * func_80B4AB40 -> EnZl1_DoNothing1
    deduced, confidence HIGH: an empty function with no arguments; the file
    has two such stubs at consecutive addresses.

  * func_80B4AB48 -> EnZl1_DoNothing2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the second of those two empty stubs.

  * func_80B4AE18 -> EnZl1_UpdateFace
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drives Zelda's blink on a randomised timer and
    picks the eye and mouth textures, holding a fixed sideways glance during
    the first frames of one animation.

  * func_80B4AF18 -> EnZl1_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tracks the player with her head and offers
    talk once he is level with her or below, running the collision check
    each frame.

  * func_80B4B010 -> EnZl1_StartCourtyardCutscene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: on the first conversation it starts her
    turn-around animation, creates the sub-camera and whites the screen out
    to open the courtyard scene.

  * func_80B4B240 -> EnZl1_CourtyardCutscene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs that scene as a numbered sequence of
    animation frames, camera moves and textboxes.

  * func_80B4B7F4 -> EnZl1_GetCueStartPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies an actor cue's start position into a
    Vec3f.

  * func_80B4B834 -> EnZl1_GetCueEndPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies an actor cue's end position into a
    Vec3f.

  * func_80B4B874 -> EnZl1_MoveActor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enables root motion on the skeleton and queues
    the animation system's actor move.

  * func_80B4B8B4 -> EnZl1_CsPlayCueAnimation
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the animation the current actor cue
    calls for and keeps Zelda on the cue's path.

  * func_80B4BBC4 -> EnZl1_StartPeepholeTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: starts her looping surprised animation, halts
    the actors, plays Link's surprise voice and opens the first line of the
    window conversation.

  * func_80B4BC78 -> EnZl1_CsFollowCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the cutscene action that keeps playing the
    cue's animation and following its path.

  * func_80B4BF2C -> EnZl1_PeepholeTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steps that window conversation through its
    numbered lines, branching on the player's choice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
